(4161458, 590367, 5885, '<td valign="top">Nice effort and not a bad score at all. Pretty good for something that is "over-sharpened and uncomfortable" with or without the foot :-)</td>', 'Nice effort and not a bad score at all. Pretty good for something that is "over-sharpened and uncomfortable" with or without the foot :-)', '2007-10-11 22:05:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4171230, 591168, 50695, '<td valign="top">It looks like you''re showing off your ability to cut an orange peel. The natural light is the best thing about it. At least that gives a hint of reality, like there might be a real person nearby who wants to eat that orange. Having a black background works against you, though, brings me back to the "showing off" idea. Showing off might work sometimes in a competition, but when it comes to creating something that actual people in the real world will care about, it won''t do.</td>', 'It looks like you''re showing off your ability to cut an orange peel. The natural light is the best thing about it. At least that gives a hint of reality, like there might be a real person nearby who wants to eat that orange. Having a black background works against you, though, brings me back to the "showing off" idea. Showing off might work sometimes in a competition, but when it comes to creating something that actual people in the real world will care about, it won''t do.', '2007-10-16 09:42:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4181463, 591649, 47933, '<td valign="top">Good eye bro and congrats on your ribbon. Creative.</td>', 'Good eye bro and congrats on your ribbon. Creative.', '2007-10-19 17:01:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4183291, 591168, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nice angling of the swirls so that they point in a diagonal across the frame.  I agree with posthumous that the black background seems jarring, not quite right.</td>', 'Nice angling of the swirls so that they point in a diagonal across the frame.  I agree with posthumous that the black background seems jarring, not quite right.', '2007-10-20 16:16:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4183373, 591077, 73601, '<td valign="top">cool blur of the car against the stillness of the grass, was this planned? or random? Like it</td>', 'cool blur of the car against the stillness of the grass, was this planned? or random? Like it', '2007-10-20 17:32:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4191263, 591786, 74242, '<td valign="top">Better luck next time :)</td>', 'Better luck next time :)', '2007-10-24 01:58:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4199662, 590597, 61651, '<td valign="top">It is perhaps a bit over-exposed, but I was really impressed by the composition overall and real sense of history you evoked.  You took the theme of "curve" to a new level.</td>', 'It is perhaps a bit over-exposed, but I was really impressed by the composition overall and real sense of history you evoked.  You took the theme of "curve" to a new level.', '2007-10-27 16:22:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4205109, 591649, 38509, '<td valign="top">congratz, nice action photo, BW is okay ...!</td>', 'congratz, nice action photo, BW is okay ...!', '2007-10-30 04:44:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4205110, 591723, 38509, '<td valign="top">yes, this is really cool photo, nice work ! congratulations</td>', 'yes, this is really cool photo, nice work ! congratulations', '2007-10-30 04:44:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4205111, 591736, 38509, '<td valign="top">nice colors, and i must say i can smell the air while looking at this photo ... really awesome feeling. congratulations !</td>', 'nice colors, and i must say i can smell the air while looking at this photo ... really awesome feeling. congratulations !', '2007-10-30 04:45:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4205113, 590224, 38509, '<td valign="top">Awesome ! simply great ...</td>', 'Awesome ! simply great ...', '2007-10-30 04:46:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4205268, 590224, 44073, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image, great sky, unique landscape!</td>', 'Wonderful image, great sky, unique landscape!', '2007-10-30 08:35:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4230172, 591325, 69008, '<td valign="top">I can see what you were shooting for here. I am not sure how to shoot this scene so that it would not be so "busy" looking, unless you shot it from ground level, with the sky behind the gate. I think that I would have moved in close if possible, and shot a small area of the gate with the wavy rod being the primary subject, in order to get the "S" curve.  The gate is  an interesting piece of art. The colors do not seem to work well with the house color behind it for me. <br/>It takes time to develop the eye for simplicity and "eye magnetism" in your images. Looking at good images posted by others will help to speed that learning curve along. <br/>Good luck with dpc and your camera. Keep shooting and posting images.</td>', 'I can see what you were shooting for here. I am not sure how to shoot this scene so that it would not be so "busy" looking, unless you shot it from ground level, with the sky behind the gate. I think that I would have moved in close if possible, and shot a small area of the gate with the wavy rod being the primary subject, in order to get the "S" curve.  The gate is  an interesting piece of art. The colors do not seem to work well with the house color behind it for me. It takes time to develop the eye for simplicity and "eye magnetism" in your images. Looking at good images posted by others will help to speed that learning curve along. Good luck with dpc and your camera. Keep shooting and posting images.', '2007-11-07 21:56:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4371050, 591649, 86056, '<td valign="top">i love this shot soo much =]</td>', 'i love this shot soo much =]', '2008-01-07 18:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4373522, 590352, 3087, '<td valign="top">A sweet image of two brothers/ friends. I like that they are walking away from us down the path - their anonymity makes the image more universal in appeal/ story. The framing of the foliage on fully three sides really makes the forest / park seem to envelop them. The path, and the way it goes from widest at the lower edge of the frame, to narrow and disappearing around a corner further back, is inviting. I find that bird feeder (assuming that''s what it is) at top right distracting and would clone it out in a non-challenge-entry version of the image. Likewise the slightly-too-strong vertical of dried branch to the right of the boys.</td>', 'A sweet image of two brothers/ friends. I like that they are walking away from us down the path - their anonymity makes the image more universal in appeal/ story. The framing of the foliage on fully three sides really makes the forest / park seem to envelop them. The path, and the way it goes from widest at the lower edge of the frame, to narrow and disappearing around a corner further back, is inviting. I find that bird feeder (assuming that''s what it is) at top right distracting and would clone it out in a non-challenge-entry version of the image. Likewise the slightly-too-strong vertical of dried branch to the right of the boys.', '2008-01-08 10:08:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4389742, 591710, 23484, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot.  This reminds me of the North Fork from the TV show Dallas. Good job.</td>', 'Excellent shot.  This reminds me of the North Fork from the TV show Dallas. Good job.', '2008-01-13 20:28:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4390741, 589908, 63267, '<td valign="top">This image is just huge.  Most of the S-Curves were so minimal compared to how vast this image seems.  Where do you infd subjects like this to photograph?  It is really an awesome photo, congrats on the finish.</td>', 'This image is just huge.  Most of the S-Curves were so minimal compared to how vast this image seems.  Where do you infd subjects like this to photograph?  It is really an awesome photo, congrats on the finish.', '2008-01-14 07:15:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4469052, 589398, 51538, '<td valign="top">By way of addition to my comment on your inquiry about stock submissions at iStock, after looking at your portfolio here:  Images like this one might well be rejected by iStock because there is a significant crackdown going on with regard to photos that do not have property or model releases.  Any model (even back views) or property depicted that is in the least bit recognizable should have a release form uploaded.</td>', 'By way of addition to my comment on your inquiry about stock submissions at iStock, after looking at your portfolio here:  Images like this one might well be rejected by iStock because there is a significant crackdown going on with regard to photos that do not have property or model releases.  Any model (even back views) or property depicted that is in the least bit recognizable should have a release form uploaded.', '2008-02-07 18:07:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4627702, 591695, 63269, '<td valign="top">Well... if it were in sharper focus, of course, that would be a bit help. Also, although I''m sure this is a rather difficult subject to get an interesting composition with, I''m not entirely sure I would crop it off like that. Also, it is slightly over-exposed and that shadow from the harsh lighting is not a good thing. I do like the bright colors with the white though - you had the right idea! ;)</td>', 'Well... if it were in sharper focus, of course, that would be a bit help. Also, although I''m sure this is a rather difficult subject to get an interesting composition with, I''m not entirely sure I would crop it off like that. Also, it is slightly over-exposed and that shadow from the harsh lighting is not a good thing. I do like the bright colors with the white though - you had the right idea! ;)', '2008-04-09 16:37:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4947976, 591532, 97522, '<td valign="top">its not even an S<br/> ... effortless</td>', 'its not even an S ... effortless', '2008-09-10 15:41:27.000000', NULL, 0);
